# Whole-project review · `guide:nrz:project-review`

## Scope and evidence · `sec:nrz:project-review-scope`

This record reviews `a817107386ff8ba45108475fe05a6d8929028a0c` on 2026-10-22. The tree contains five engine crates and `tools/docgen`, with no `nrz-physics`. Its strongest established boundary is independent checking of exact symbolic answers and numerical matrix candidates. Immediate constraints are proof-checking cost, incomplete algebraic consequence discovery, and the gap between checked heterogeneous shapes and executable homogeneous regions. The quantity-facing integration and reusable physics plans remain ahead.

**Convention (Evidence and audit scope)** · `conv:nrz:project-review-evidence`

Paths are relative to the repository root. In the CAS inventory, `solving/` abbreviates `crates/cas/src/solving/`; unqualified checker filenames abbreviate `crates/cas/src/`. The audit follows public entry points, closed inventories, checker dispatch, dependency traversal, refusal paths and tests. It is source review and regression evidence, not a machine-checked metatheorem. An available checker is distinguished from an automatic producer, and a represented payload from an accepted theorem. Conditional witnesses retain their assumptions and residuals.

New execution measurements are diagnostics on sojka on 2026-10-22 against the seed, with disposable instrumentation excluded from the commit. Diagnostic 1 runs workspace tests with per-test timing and forced function-length Clippy checking. Diagnostics 2–3 measure existing symbolic fixtures with original coefficient order `d,c,b,a`, separating generation, production checking and fresh expected-judgment replay. Diagnostic 4 attributes application checking by primitive; diagnostic 5 reproduces a nested-root remainder. Static counts describe tracked seed files, including comments and blank lines. Historical measurements retain their original environment and profile; charged work and elapsed time are different quantities.

