## CAS trust base · `sec:nrz:project-review-trust`

**Argument (Independent checking and its trusted implementation)** · `arg:nrz:project-review-checker`

`scoped_check.rs::preflight` requires backward premises, complete reachability from the final application and available rules. `check_application` measures the draft, checks coefficient scope, dispatches the closed rule, unions conditions, validates hypothesis ancestry and validates the judgment before publication. The scalar fast path still runs `proof_check.rs::compile`. Admission/replay is transactional. `wire_decode.rs::inspect` reconstructs typed dependencies and applications; canonical re-encoding rejects unused or noncanonical records. `Cas::replay` compares the complete expected context, layer, space, statement and residual tuple through `wire_build.rs::judgment_key`. Inspection proves the imported theorem; only expected-judgment comparison binds it to the caller's intended theorem.

Trusted code includes admission, scope/dependency traversal, exact arithmetic, finite checker rules, encoding/decoding and the execution environment. Producer and checker share arithmetic infrastructure; independence means reconstruction from untrusted certificates, not independent arithmetic implementations. Mathematical assumptions include the admitted characteristic-zero field laws, ordered Real laws, Complex closure/FTA, primitive unity, Real odd/positive-square roots, Sturm counting and the explicit calculus/distribution laws below. No producer success flag or serialized truth bit replaces those checks. This audit found no accepted rule bypass in the closed dispatch; unavailable schemas and conditional hypotheses remain explicit qualifications.

`rule.rs::PRIMITIVES` contains 80 entries: 59 general and 21 solving keys. There are 78 executable entries: solving tags 15 and 17 are unavailable. Retained schemas use version 1, policy is `logical` v10 and the sole envelope is `NRZCAS04`. Removed tag 13 (`RealRestriction`) has no compatibility reader (`rule.rs`, `solving/{registry,wire}.rs`, `solving/isolation/mod.rs`, `solving/local/mod.rs`). Registry membership and policy weight are not theorem authority.

